 "assumptions": [
  "L is the patch-row count: 49+144+ceil(W/32)*ceil(H/32), including the padded fixed-scale groups even for rectangular images. The transformer appends one class token, so T=L+1. The patch stem and embedding run on L; all 14 transformer blocks and final layer norm run on T.",
  "Frozen musiq.onnx and models/musiq/export.py: root 7x7 stride-2 conv maps a padded 32x32 patch to 16x16. Then padded 3x3 stride-2 max-pool gives 8x8. Conv1, Conv2, Conv3 and Conv-proj therefore run at 8x8, not 16x16. Stem MACs per patch = 7127040; embedding MACs = 16384*384.",
  "Each block has 3 qkv and 1 output projections at 384x384 plus 384->1152->384 MLP: 1474560 MACs/token/block. Both attention matmuls contribute 2*384*T*T MACs/block. The scalar head uses only CLS (384 MACs plus bias).",
  "Logical affine group/layer norm uses add=4*d-1, mul=2*d, div=d+2, sqrt=1 per normalized row. Stem groups: three 512-element and two 128-element rows per each of 32 groups per patch. Tanh GELU uses the exported six Mul, two Add and one Tanh per 1152-wide activation; Tanh uses trig class. Stable softmax uses add=2*T-1, cmp=T-1, exp=T, div=T per attention row.",
  "Partial tally: Gaussian resize weight generation and resampling arithmetic, spatial-hash construction, activation/matrix traffic and global attention halo/span are not derived. Patch-row load/store is logical payload only, including zero padding. Ingress normalizes all original RGB samples. Counts are graph/source logical work, not engine instructions.",
  "The scorer refuses L>8192 and degenerate resized axes before inference. In particular the standard 3840x2160 evaluator point has L=8353 and is outside the accepted domain; its reported arithmetic is diagnostic extrapolation only. This schema does not encode refusal, so callers must retain this qualification."
 ],
